<title>FRANCE: Sanofi 1996 net rises 11 percent.</title>
<headline>Sanofi 1996 net rises 11 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net earnings				 1,743  vs 1,575</p>
<p>Net attributable per share (francs)  16.80  up eight percent</p>
<p>    Operating				    3,531  vs	   3,427</p>
<p>    Cashflow    (billions)		     3.1  up 12 percent</p>
<p>    Investments (billions)		     2.8  vs no comparison</p>
<p>    Turnover				    23,645  vs	  23,031</p>
<p>    R&amp;D spending				 3,253  vs	   3,105</p>
<p>NOTE - Sanofi gave its results in a statement. It said net earnings rose 11 percent over the year ago period. Net debt to equity ratio at the end of 1996 was 11 percent versus 13 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
